  "body": "UMR-20260805-165906-0923 (child of UMR-20260802-165606-4413 / OCID-020), executed per PM instruction UMR-20260805-171657-01de.\n\n## What\n- `gtm_check_ui_testing.py` (category_index=5, \"UI testing\"): new minimal Playwright probe against real, live `https://projexa-ai.com/login` and `/signup`. Confirms expected form controls (#email, #password, #fullName, #org, submit) are present, visible, and enabled, with zero page/console errors. Never fills or submits any field -- no dedicated UI spec existed in compliance-tracker's `e2e/`, so this is new per the dispatching task's own fallback rule.\n- `gtm_check_e2e_testing.py` (category_index=6, \"end to end testing\"): reuses the existing real `e2e/browser-execution-tiers.spec.ts` via `npx playwright test e2e/ --reporter=json`.\n- `gtm_write_category_result.py`: shared canonical writer, carried over unchanged (this repo's open GTM PRs are independent, not stacked).\n\n## Real results\n- Category 5: **pass** -- both pages HTTP 200, all expected controls present/visible/enabled, 0 page/console errors.\n- Category 6: **pass** -- `expected=1, unexpected=0, skipped=0, flaky=0`, exit 0.\n\nBoth rows independently re-read directly from `superboss-register.sqlite` after write (not trusted from script stdout alone).\n\n## Safety verification (Hard Rule 8 / file_inventory)\nBefore any DB write this session: grepped `gtm_write_category_result.py` and `superboss-register.py`'s `_connect()`/`_write_lock()` directly -- zero references to `file_inventory` (the one real, confirmed-corrupted table held for Owner recovery decision). No whole-database `PRAGMA integrity_check` was run; only a scoped read-only probe reconfirming `file_inventory` alone still fails, matching the standing hold.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
